  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baringo-FGM phase 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall aim of this project is to accelerate abandonment of female genital mutilation (FGM)   among young girls and women. This will be achieved through a unified front of government accountability, community oversight, and faith-based leadership, ensuring that:
&#x2022;	Duty bearers and political leaders at the county and sub-county levels effectively implement, track, and sustain FGM abandonment, through sustained budgetary allocations and enforced accountability frameworks.
&#x2022;	Rights holders and community-led networks (youth groups, local committees) independently monitor and influence FGM policy implementation. 
&#x2022;	FPFK and local leadership networks (government administrators, community elders) actively champion Alternative Rites of Passage (ARP) and advocate for total FGM abandonment in the targeted area.The</narrative>
  </description>
